      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"innovation and better decision making\" argument is largely based on anecdotal evidence and unreplicable studies, often cherry-picked to support a preconceived narrative. A 2019 study by McKinsey found that companies with more diverse workforces are more likely to outperform their less diverse peers, but this was largely due to the fact that these companies were already more successful and had more resources to invest in DEI initiatives. In reality, the evidence is far from conclusive, and many studies have found no significant correlation between diversity and business outcomes.",
      "source": "target",
